# NO ARTWORK IS EVER COMMITTED, OF EITHER KIND. The regenerated pages the captain
# uploads against one order are a picture of one family's child, this
# repository is public, and git history is permanent — a file committed by
# mistake and deleted in the next commit is still there, still fetchable, for
# good. `lib/artwork/store.ts` § DEFAULT_ARTWORK_DIR writes here and
# `test/order-artwork.test.ts` asserts this rule, because a gitignore line is a
# one-line thing to lose in a merge and this is the one whose loss cannot be
# undone. ORDER_ARTWORK_DIR may point anywhere outside the tree instead.
#
# THE CAPTAIN'S RELEASED ARTWORK IS IN HERE TOO, under `release/`, for a
# different reason that lands in the same place: one look of twenty-four
# finished pages is 155 MB and twelve looks is the better part of two
# gigabytes, which nobody should have to clone. `lib/artwork/release.ts` says
# why not even its manifest is committed, and `RELEASE_ARTWORK_DIR` moves it.
# One rule covers both, so there is only one line here to lose in a merge.
.artwork/
